+	/* GORILLA UNLEASHED: an access point does not get to turn this radio
+	 * down. Stock mac80211 obeys both the 802.11h Power Constraint IE and
+	 * Cisco's DTPC IE, which on 2026-08-10 logged
+	 *   "Limiting TX power to 20 (20 - 0) dBm as advertised by <bssid>"
+	 * immediately after association. Returning 0 leaves link->ap_power_level
+	 * untouched, so __ieee80211_recalc_txpower() keeps the driver/regulatory
+	 * figure instead of the AP's. The radio is still bounded by hardware
+	 * calibration and by chan->max_power; this only removes the AP's vote.
+	 *
+	 * The code below is intentionally retained (unreachable) so the upstream
+	 * logic stays readable and easy to restore. Rationale: docs/regd.c.md. */
+	return 0;
